Insert into TNO.NEWS_ITEMS (RSN,ITEM_DATE,SOURCE,ITEM_TIME,SUMMARY,TITLE,TYPE,FRONTPAGESTORY,PUBLISHED,ARCHIVED,ARCHIVED_TO,RECORD_CREATED,RECORD_MODIFIED,STRING1,STRING2,STRING3,STRING4,STRING5,STRING6,STRING7,STRING8,STRING9,NUMBER1,NUMBER2,DATE1,DATE2,FILENAME,FULLFILEPATH,WEBPATH,THISJUSTIN,IMPORTEDFROM,EXPIRE_RULE,COMMENTARY,CONTENTTYPE,BINARYLOADED,LOADBINARY,EXTERNALBINARY,CBRA_NONQSM,POSTEDBY,ONTICKER,WAPTOPSTORY,ALERT,AUTO_TONE,CATEGORIES_LOCKED,CORE_ALERT,COMMENTARY_TIMEOUT,COMMENTARY_EXPIRE_TIME,EOD_CATEGORY,EOD_CATEGORY_GROUP,EOD_DATE) values (778307262,to_date('19-MAY-23','DD-MON-RR'),'BiV',to_date('01-JAN-70','DD-MON-RR'),'At the heart of British Columbia''s economic saga unfolds a narrative, the tale of the province''s bold attempt to impose an "output-based pricing system" (OBPS) on greenhouse gasses.' || CHR(13) || CHR(10) || CHR(13) || CHR(10) || 'Picture a menu, where each CO2 emission - an uninvited but hard-to-escape by-product of business operations - comes with a price. Commendable? Certainly. But amid the cheers for such environmental stewardship, a subplot of potential economic turbulence arises, casting long shadows over the employment landscape of B.C.' || CHR(13) || CHR(10) || CHR(13) || CHR(10) || 'Visualize a B.C. saw mill, churning out lumber to build homes near and far. For the past 15 years since B.C. became one of the first jurisdictions anywhere in the world to adopt a carbon tax, each release of CO2 comes with a growing bill.' || CHR(13) || CHR(10) || CHR(13) || CHR(10) || 'Now, throw in a twist: imagine a lumber mill in the United States that gets to whistle while it works, free of any carbon-tax yoke. Suddenly, our virtuous B.C. lumber mill is the underdog, its product potentially seen as too costly in comparison to its counterpart''s offerings.' || CHR(13) || CHR(10) || CHR(13) || CHR(10) || 'Imagine a smelter in a faraway corner of the world, producing metal using the cheapest and dirtiest fuels, and the laugh they are having at the sight of their green-powered British Columbia competitors being squeezed out of business for the crime of being not green enough.' || CHR(13) || CHR(10) || CHR(13) || CHR(10) || 'In the cutthroat world of global commerce, being costlier equates to being less attractive. It''s somewhat like the class valedictorian being penalized for diligently following the rules while the schoolyard bully gets off scot-free.' || CHR(13) || CHR(10) || CHR(13) || CHR(10) || 'This ominous trend isn''t a fantasy. Only a few months ago, Parkland Refinery packed its bags, abandoning a green project in Vancouver for greener pastures down south, where investor incentives glittered enticingly.' || CHR(13) || CHR(10) || CHR(13) || CHR(10) || 'If doing business in B.C. becomes synonymous with shelling out more due to carbon costs, what stops others from taking the Parkland route?' || CHR(13) || CHR(10) || CHR(13) || CHR(10) || 'An eco-conscious policy, while noble, could inadvertently cause economic fallout.','The high price of being a Green Canadian','Internet',1,1,0,null,to_date('19-MAY-23','DD-MON-RR'),to_date('19-MAY-23','DD-MON-RR'),null,null,null,'column','Stewart Muir','Stewart Muir',null,null,null,0,0,null,to_date('01-JAN-70','DD-MON-RR'),null,null,'http://biv.com/article/2023/05/stewart-muir-high-price-being-green-canadian',0,null,0,0,null,0,0,0,0,'rfreeman',0,0,0,null,0,0,0,0,null,null,null);
